WEBVTT

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.230
Congratulations on winning the first round!

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.770
Thank you very much!

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:17.940
Among the fans, you are called the return
of Miss Mana, who was once your senior.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.270
What?

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.940
Um...

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.440
Is this something you're conscious of?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.980
I don't really understand it myself,

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.650
but when I sing with the voice
that feels best,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.150
people tell me that I sound like Miss Mana.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.730
She's a senior I respect,
so it makes me feel happy!

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.350
That was a good bath.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.690
Kotono?

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.230
Can we talk?

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.560
This is about my sister's song
I mentioned before.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.440
The song Miss Mana was supposed
to sing for her last finals performance?

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.940
Yeah.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.560
There's something I wanted to tell you.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.400
Three years ago...

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:42.310
The day before the final round,
the last night I spoke with my sister...

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:46.310
I said something terrible
to my sister after she told me

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.770
she wanted me to go watch
her final performance.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.770
Feelings I'd been concealing deep in my heart...

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:57.980
Turned into words and ended up hurting her...

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.770
I despised myself for it, and was
depressed and alone in my room.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.850
Kotono.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.850
So... you still won't come
see my performance?

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.060
All right.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.310
Well, it's not fun or anything watching a family
member who you see all the time singing, right?

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:27.770
Then, can you listen to this song, at least?

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.730
I'm singing it for the first time
at the finals tomorrow.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.520
You're the first one to hear it, Kotono.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.650
I only heard it once.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.600
But I can still remember it vividly.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.480
That song was so wonderful,

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.270
and it warms your heart
when you listen to it.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.440
So I wanted to ask you again,

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.440
Sakura...

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.060
Sing my sister's song at the Grand Prix.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.590
Hoshimi Productions

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.590
Hoshimi Productions

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.590
Hoshimi Productions

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.590
Hoshimi Productions

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.940
Miss Mana's unreleased song?!

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.980
It's true that Mana was supposed to sing
that song for her finals performance.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.850
How did you know about that?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.440
Big Sister told me.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.560
She told me directly the day
before the performance.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.600
It's a very wonderful song,

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.980
and it warms you up just listening to it.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.770
I've got the data for the song.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.190
But I don't have a recording
of Mana singing it.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.150
It was before we recorded it.

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.100
So it really is a legendary song...

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.060
I've heard from Mr. Saegusa...

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:41.520
I still remember how my sister sang it.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.400
I'll teach her,

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.350
so what if we had Sakura sing that song?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.230
Right now...

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:53.020
I think Sakura... Sunny Peace
has the ability to sing it.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.850
Kotono...

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:59.150
I'll leave the final decision up to you,
Mr. Makino and Sunny Peace.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.020
That song, huh?

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.850
I agree that Sakura
might be able to pull it off.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:11.520
What do you think, Mr. Saegusa?

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.520
You're the one in charge.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.810
So far,

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:22.230
it could be a little softer.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.650
What's up?

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.440
If you suggested this a little while ago,
I think I would've declined.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:36.100
Well, because... singing this song on stage in
place of Miss Mana was your goal, right, Kotono?

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:41.770
If I had sung it instead, I would have worried
that you would lose your purpose.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.400
But after watching your last performance,
my thinking totally changed.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.230
My last performance?

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.520
Yup!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.690
Kotono, when you were on that stage,

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.190
I don't know how to say this exactly, but...

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:58.600
It really seemed like
Kotono of Moon Tempest!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.520
And plus,

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.100
my heart is beating fast again.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:07.020
It's telling me to sing this song.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.690
So right now,

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:12.100
I can confidently take on Miss Mana's song.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.060
This one would look great on you, Sakura.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.940
--Aw, thanks.
--I see.
--As for me...

